<h2>Indian dehydrated onion for export</h2>
<p>We process cured onion into kibbled pieces, flakes, granules and powder for food manufacturers worldwide. This is genuinely one of our best-diversified product lines — around 120 destination markets in our 2024 data, with the USA, Brazil and Germany leading a list that also includes Indonesia, Belgium, the UK, Russia, the Netherlands, Spain and Canada.</p>

<p>Processing plants sit in Maharashtra and Gujarat, close to the Nashik/Ahmednagar fresh-onion belt that supplies raw material. Peak processing runs March through September on the rabi-season harvest, though finished product stores well enough to ship year-round.</p>

<h2>Why dehydrated onion is a pricing-stable alternative to fresh</h2>
<p>This deserves its own section because it's the single most useful thing to understand about this product relative to fresh onion. Fresh onion (HS 0703.10) is one of India's most actively policy-managed exports — a Minimum Export Price, at times an export duty, and even a full export ban in 2023–24 have all applied. Dehydrated onion, classified separately under HS 0712.20, carries none of that. Export policy here is simply Free, with no MEP mechanism attached.</p>
<p>For buyers who need predictable, quotable pricing months in advance — rather than terms that must be reconfirmed against whatever Indian policy happens to say that week — dehydrated onion is a genuinely different proposition from fresh, not just a processed version of the same risk. See our detailed <a href="/blog/dehydrated-onion-vs-fresh-onion-mep/">dehydrated vs fresh onion comparison</a> for the full breakdown.</p>

<h2>How should I specify dehydrated onion?</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Form.</strong> Kibbled, flakes, granules or powder — each suits different applications (seasoning blends vs. instant foods vs. snack coatings).</li>
  <li><strong>Mesh/particle size.</strong> Specify your target range; finer grades cost more to produce and are priced accordingly.</li>
  <li><strong>Moisture.</strong> ≤5–6% is standard export tolerance — lower moisture means longer shelf life and less clumping risk.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Dehydrated onion export pricing</h2>
<p>Send your form, mesh size, quantity and destination port and we'll quote current FOB/CIF terms within 24 business hours — with a longer validity window than we can offer on fresh onion, precisely because the policy backdrop is stable.</p>

